From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wbemprox: SystemRestore methods keep real state (3660)

wbemprox: SystemRestore methods keep real state

CreateRestorePoint records the point (description, type, event type, time)
under a sequence number kept in the registry and validates its parameters,
Enable and Disable record the drive state, GetLastRestoreStatus returns the
recorded status, and Restore reports an unknown point or that a known one
cannot be applied. All methods now return their ReturnValue out parameter
(the signatures for CreateRestorePoint, GetLastRestoreStatus and Restore
were missing). An unknown system property name is a WARN, not a FIXME.
---
